WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.920
For the 33rd movie in the MCU, "The Marvels"
is a surprisingly light and wacky cosmic adventure.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.720
But the ending still has massive ramifications
for the future of Marvel on the big screen.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:18.239
At the start of "The Marvels," our three leads
are in very different places — both emotionally and physically.

00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:23.039
Kamala is riding high off of her heroic ascent
at the end of "Ms. Marvel," drawing fresh

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:27.270
fan art of herself and Captain Marvel in her
Jersey City bedroom.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.400
Monica is investigating a strange energy phenomenon
aboard the S.A.B.E.R.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.560
space station orbiting Earth, and Carol is,
as usual, alone — riding through the empty

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:40.149
blackness of the cosmos with no one but Goose
at her side.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:45.260
After the Kree warrior Dar-Benn locates a
powerful bangle just like Kamala's, she begins

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.919
tearing holes in space-time to restore the
Kree homeworld of Hala to glory.

00:00:49.919 --> 00:00:54.329
This causes the three heroes' abilities to
become entangled, meaning that whenever two

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:56.989
of them power up at the same time, they swap
places.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.840
"What is happening to me?"

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.890
The ensuing chaos brings Kamala face-to-face
with her idol and Monica face-to-face with

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.500
the aunt who abandoned her.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.320
Together, they try to stop Dar-Benn from stealing
various planets' resources, with mixed results.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.810
They do manage to confront some of their own
demons, however, preparing them for a showdown

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.401
with Dar-Benn on Earth.

00:01:17.401 --> 00:01:23.760
As her crowning move, she aims to steal Kamala's
bangle and use the amplified power to take our sun.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.050
But she has to get through the Marvels first.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:26.550
"We're a team?"

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.550
"Oh no no no no.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.550
We're not a team."

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:31.970
As Dar-Benn begins her attack over Earth,
the S.A.B.E.R.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:34.080
station starts to destabilize.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.259
But with many core systems already knocked
out, there aren't enough escape pods to get

00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:39.810
everyone to safety.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:44.550
Thankfully, Goose comes in clutch by birthing
a horde of Flerken kittens about the station.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.102
"Oh my god!"

00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:51.619
When the Marvels arrive, they help Nick Fury
chase down all the S.A.B.E.R.

00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:54.590
folks so that the Flerkens can gobble them
up.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:59.189
This stores them in the kitties' void-like
tummies, effectively shrinking the population

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:04.049
of the station and allowing them to fit (inside
the cats) in the remaining pods.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:09.030
It's a bizarre and hilarious sequence aptly
set to "Memory" from the musical, "Cats,"

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.060
but rest assured, everyone is regurgitated
safely on the ground.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.060
"I can't.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.060
Can you?"

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.910
"I got it."

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:20.280
Meanwhile, Kamala, Carol, and Monica face
off against Dar-Benn.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.410
They defeat her, and Carol agrees to a tentative
peace.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.269
She promises to use her powers to restore
Hala's sun, undoing the damage unintentionally

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:32.290
wrought by her destruction of the Supreme
Intelligence in "Captain Marvel."

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:38.830
Of course, Dar-Benn double-crosses them, steals
Kamala's bangle, and launches herself into the void.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:43.370
With both "quantum bands," Dar-Benn rips a
hole in space-time clean through to an alternate

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.410
reality, vaporizing herself in the process.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:51.280
Carol retrieves the bangles, gives them both
to Kamala and together, they power up Monica

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.930
enough that she can fly to the other side
of the hole and close it.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:59.690
Tragically, though, she's trapped there, as
Carol can't save her in time.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:04.970
With Earth saved, Dar-Benn defeated, and Monica
lost in some strange unknown, Carol decides

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.670
to finally settle her battle with the Kree.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.310
She returns to Hala, where the dying sun barely
lights the sky anymore.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:16.409
Then, in a staggering display of her power,
she flies straight through the star, energizing

00:03:16.409 --> 00:03:21.239
its core reactions with her energy and reviving
it to its bright, glowing glory.

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:26.719
The Annihilator, as the Kree calls her throughout
the movie, becomes the savior of the entire race.

00:03:26.719 --> 00:03:29.120
For Captain Marvel, this is a big deal.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.700
She reveals throughout the film that her conflict
with the Kree still largely defines her life.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:38.239
The violence they committed against her alienated
her from everyone she once knew as family.

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:43.260
At the same time, her vengeance against them
only led to more violence, as the entire world

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.450
of Hala fell into a quick decline.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:51.060
By repairing Hala's sun, Carol shows that
she can be a force for creation as well as destruction.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:55.810
This closure, combined with her experiences
with Kamala and Monica, finally allows her

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.530
to move on and return home to Earth.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:02.709
This could also finally mark the end of the
longstanding Kree-Skrull conflict.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:07.280
The movie suggests that both species are finally
ready to invest in peace, and the healing

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.340
of Hala might be all the Kree needed to give
up on their evil crusade at last.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.519
With her Kree chapter finally closed, Carol
goes home.

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:19.510
Or, rather, she goes to a new home, but one
that's very familiar.

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:24.560
We see the Kahn family help her move into
Maria and Monica Rambeau's old house in Louisiana

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.870
from the first "Captain Marvel" movie.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:32.359
Dressed in regular Earth attire, Carol finally
seems ready to stop moving around for a little bit.

00:04:32.359 --> 00:04:37.370
Throughout the movie, we learn how much guilt
she carries from her time with and fighting the Kree.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:41.919
But now that she's made peace with that part
of her past, she decides to stop running.

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.000
Of course, she has an ulterior motive in moving
into the old Rambeau house.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.230
As she tells Kamala, she's just taking care
of it while she waits for Monica to "get back."

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:56.700
She has no idea where Monica could be or whether
she'll ever return, but that doesn't dissuade

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:57.780
her from staying.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.220
Even with Monica gone, she's not going to
abandon her again.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:02.720
In another scene on the S.A.B.E.R.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.870
station, we see that Fury misses her too.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:10.570
The final scene of "The Marvels" takes place
in New York City, where Kamala confronts none

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.040
other than Kate Bishop.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.500
"Hawkeye sent me here on official Avengers
business.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.750
I'm his partner-slash-best friend, Kate."

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:21.130
The whole thing plays like a spoof of the
Nick Fury post-credit scene from "Iron Man,"

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:25.960
as Kate comes home to find Kamala sitting
in an armchair, cloaked in darkness.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:32.180
Kamala puts on her best Fury impression, but
it quickly gives way to her own fast-talking, quirky persona.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.460
She tells Kate that she's putting together
a team, which, at the moment, is just the

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.030
two of them — provided Kate accepts.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:43.440
She assures her, though, that she has "feelers"
out there, mentioning Ant-Man's daughter Cassie

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.940
Lang specifically.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:50.370
Despite the somewhat clumsy proposal, Kate
smiles, suggesting that she's down for the team-up.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:54.470
This seems like an obvious setup for the oft-theorized
"Young Avengers" movie.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.010
The MCU has introduced a ton of new heroes
in Phase 4 and Phase 5.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:04.030
Any combination of these characters and others
could form a new superhero team, and the ending

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.189
of "The Marvels" seems to set that up perfectly.

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:11.509
There's only one credits scene in "The Marvels,"
positioned between the first round of main

00:06:11.509 --> 00:06:14.250
credits and the standard credits that come
after.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:19.701
In it, we see Monica awaken in some kind of
medical facility, groggy but alive after her

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:20.521
cosmic outing.

00:06:20.521 --> 00:06:25.190
She turns and sees none other than her own
mother sitting at her bedside — albeit a

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.009
pretty young version of her.

00:06:27.009 --> 00:06:31.669
When Monica calls Maria "Mom," the older woman
looks at her strangely, suggesting that she's

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:33.410
never seen Monica before.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:38.530
Then, everything gets turned on its head when
Kelsey Grammer's Hank McCoy, aka Beast, walks

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:42.819
into frame -- fully blue, furry, and dressed
in a lab coat.

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:47.090
Outside the glass walls of the medical room,
we can see the iconic round "X" doorway from

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.409
the X-Men movies.

00:06:48.409 --> 00:06:53.760
This and Grammer's presence both suggest that
we are in some version of the Fox X-Men universe,

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:58.580
as Grammer played Beast all the way back in
2006's "X-Men: The Last Stand."

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.580
"Strong theory!"

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:04.340
He mentions that "Charles" will want an update
on their guest, and in the last shot, we see

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:09.789
Maria's new superhero costume: a red jumpsuit
that evokes the comic book character Binary.

00:07:09.789 --> 00:07:14.199
Binary has a strange and powerful connection
to Carol Danvers in the Marvel comics, as

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:16.870
they're one in the same (it's complicated).

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:21.830
It should be interesting to see how this new
version of the character plays into the MCU's

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.660
X-Men storyline.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:27.250
The ending of "The Marvels" is more about
the action beats and future setups than it

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.481
is about larger themes or ideas.

00:07:29.481 --> 00:07:33.790
But that's not to say that the film is devoid
of meaning — quite the contrary.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.229
By the end, the biggest resounding theme — as
it is in so many modern blockbusters — is

00:07:38.229 --> 00:07:41.380
the importance of family, be it born or found.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.009
All three main characters have arcs relating
to family.

00:07:44.009 --> 00:07:48.410
At the beginning of the movie, Carol has cut
herself off from all forms of family.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:52.819
She carries so much shame and guilt that she
believes she deserves to be lonely, and she's

00:07:52.819 --> 00:07:56.449
scared of getting close to anyone again because
of the fear that she'll lose them.

00:07:56.449 --> 00:08:01.430
Of course, in the end, it's her reunion with
Monica and her new relationship with Kamala

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.790
that allows her to heal.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:08.060
Monica, likewise, has built a wall of professionalism
around herself, resentful of Carol and scared

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:10.900
to get close to anyone after the death of
her mother.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:15.130
In the end, she saves the entire world (and
possibly the universe?) because she trusts

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.819
the other two Marvels.

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:21.190
Kamala is the only one of the three who already
has a strong family, and we see just how much

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.240
that empowers her.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.900
Though her mother is always scared for her,
she ultimately accepts that Kamala is destined

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.190
for "something greater."

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:34.310
She encourages her daughter to be a hero but
also reminds her that she'll never "let her go."

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.750
"The Marvels" isn't really "Captain Marvel
2," but it does give more closure to Carol's

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.200
story than it does to Kamala's or Monica's.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.050
The latter is now stuck in a whole new reality,
and the former is just beginning what's hopefully

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.880
a long and successful superhero career.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.160
Carol doesn't retire by any means at the end
of the movie, but she does wrap up the arc

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:55.360
that began back in the first "Captain Marvel."

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.220
For decades, Carol tried to repair her memories
and reclaim her life, but she did so alone

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.000
in the cold vacuum of space.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.490
It's clear she viewed this as penance, but
she can't heal properly until she lets people

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:07.920
back into her life.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:12.839
At one point Kamala tells Carol that she made
a tough call because that's what Carol would have done.

00:09:12.839 --> 00:09:17.430
"You shouldn't try to be like me," Carol says
in response, full of self-loathing.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:22.029
Maybe it's reconciling with Monica that gets
her over that hump, or it's Kamala's unabashed

00:09:22.029 --> 00:09:23.300
reverence for her.

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:26.500
Perhaps it's the realization that she can
use her powers to heal.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:32.350
Really, it's a combination of all those things
that allows Carol to finally forgive herself.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:37.070
As fun as "The Marvels" is on its own merits,
many fans will likely be even more excited

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.430
by the future projects it may be setting up.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.310
The biggest of those is the long-awaited MCU
version of the X-Men.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:47.870
Most likely, Marvel Studios will want to make
its own X-Men movies, but the story could

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.060
also take place (at least in part) on Disney+.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.050
The slow rollout of these new X-Men has confused
things a bit as well.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:59.920
We got Patrick Stewart back as Charles Xavier
in "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,"

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:04.980
Kelsey Grammer's Beast appears in "The Marvels,"
and Hugh Jackman is set to return as Wolverine

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.190
in "Deadpool 3."

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.190
"You have questions!"

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:12.500
But as long as the multiverse era of the MCU
continues, there's no way to know how important

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.300
those actors will remain.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:18.211
Disney would probably want to fully recast
the X-Men for a new generation.

00:10:18.211 --> 00:10:20.380
For now, fans will have to keep waiting.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:25.060
The other big thing set up in "The Marvels"
is the potential "Young Avengers" project,

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:29.040
or whatever the team that Kamala Khan and
Kate Bishop are forming will be called.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:34.700
Embracing the franchise's younger heroes could
be a great way to softly reset the MCU, but

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.210
that's also a big risk.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:40.240
The one thing that "The Marvels" doesn't clearly
set up is a "Captain Marvel 3."

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.380
But that doesn't mean that it won't happen.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:47.229
Carol Danvers is back on Earth now, so she
could be pulled into any number of upcoming stories.

00:10:47.229 --> 00:10:52.560
Her new Louisiana home places her in close
proximity to Sam Wilson and his family, who

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.349
also reside in the state.

00:10:54.349 --> 00:10:58.480
Perhaps we'll get a Captain Marvel cameo in
"Captain America: Brave New World."

